#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063956 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72f03bd5-4e2c-5d8c-9d08-129fb9949a3c" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Negative Number From a Positive Number"}] :question/id #uuid "18486b46-10bc-5e64-b1d9-df3ba0736b05" :question/math-academy-id "e-13262" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $0-(-6)$." :question/worked-solution "To subtract $-6$ from $0$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 - (-6) &=  \\\\\n0 + 6 &=  \\\\\n&= 6 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/a7/a793deb0faa2f175a7f9bddc13dcff381b48aaee40b6082bd320a8748d8c8c37.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063957 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064351 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ac4d4f6-ade4-59d0-a633-fac839543b23" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Negative Number From a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "1c75cfa3-630e-5b37-82c0-ec421bb8c206" :question/math-academy-id "e-13263" :question/problem "Subtract $-100$ from $-85$." :question/worked-solution "To subtract $-100$ from $-85$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-85 - (-100) &=  \\\\\n- 85 + 100 &=  \\\\\n&= 15 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063958 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064352 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "430390f1-fd74-564c-a8d6-3925ba8b1832" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Negative Decimal From a Number"}] :question/id #uuid "735b7c5c-68c6-51b9-b3c0-cc38a4e59e95" :question/math-academy-id "e-13264" :question/problem "What is the value of $-3-(-1.5)$?" :question/worked-solution "To subtract $-1.5$ from $-3$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n-3 - (-1.5) =-3 + 1.5\n$$\n\nTo calculate $-3+1.5$, we start at $-3$ and move $1$ place to the right. Then, we move another $0.5$ places to the right:\n\n![](images/f8/f8ebeccc7db234acc592ffd79aeeb92ce5ce5a756c4500019a1c5316f78d640d.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-3-(-1.5)= -1.5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063959 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064353 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "801cc9bd-b65c-5a79-873b-ee4c5bffdc6e" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Negative Fraction From a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "347baa8c-4ba0-559a-a5b6-81e024054af6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13265" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{3}{7} - \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{7} \\right)$." :question/worked-solution "To subtract\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{11}{7}\n$$\n\nfrom\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{7}\n$$\n\nwe combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{7} - (-\\frac{11}{7}) &= \\frac{3}{7} + \\frac{11}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a common denominator of $7$, so we combine numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7} + \\frac{11}{7} = \\frac{3 + 11}{7} = \\frac{14}{7}\n$$\n\nNow, we can simplify the resulting fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{14}{7} &= 14 \\div 7 = 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator first and *then* add or subtract!"}]}
